 <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,651.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NNPCL Posts ₦535bn June Profit, Remits ₦6.3tn to Federation Accounts\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited (NNPC Ltd.) posted a profit after tax of ₦535 billion in June 2026. This was despite a marginal decline in crude oil and condensate production during the period. The company attributed the marginal production decline to operational disruptions and facility integrity challenges.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nnpcl-posts-535bn-june-profit-remits-63tn-to-federation-accounts\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Crude Returns to $90 as Fresh Iran Strikes Renew Supply Fears\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $90.02 per barrel on Friday, up 1.11 percent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) rose 1.64 percent to $84.96 per barrel. Despite Friday's gains, both Brent and WTI remain below the peaks recorded earlier this year.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-crude-returns-to-90-as-fresh-iran-strikes-renew-supply-fears\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria Removes Import Duty, VAT on Fully Gas-Powered, Electric Vehicles\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Vehicles running on compressed natural gas, liquefied petroleum gas or electric power will now enter Nigeria free of import duty and Value Added Tax. The exemption covers vehicles running entirely on CNG or LPG, battery electric vehicles, and Extended Range Electric Vehicles able to travel at least 200 kilometres on battery power alone. Hybrids remain excluded, along with dual fuel vehicles still running partly on petrol or diesel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigeria-removes-import-duty-vat-on-fully-gas-powered-electric-vehicles\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NNPCL Confirms Deployment of Over 1,000 Graduate Trainees After One-Year Programme\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited (NNPCL) has confirmed the deployment of more than 1,000 young professionals into its workforce. The milestone was announced by the Group Chief Executive Officer of NNPCL, Bayo Ojulari. He described the exercise as part of the company's ongoing efforts to build a skilled and performance-driven workforce.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nnpcl-confirms-deployment-of-over-1000-graduate-trainees-after-one-year-programme\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Seplat to Sell 10% JV Stake to NNPC in $281.6m Deal, Retains Operatorship\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Seplat Energy Plc has entered into a binding agreement to divest a 10 percent working interest in its joint venture assets to the Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited. The agreement takes effect from April 1, 2026. Seplat said proceeds from the transaction will strengthen its financial position, with about half earmarked for debt reduction.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/seplat-to-sell-10-jv-stake-to-nnpc-in-2816m-deal-retains-operatorship\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
